uw-ttyp0

UW ttyp0 is a family of monospaced bitmap screen fonts for X11 and the
Linux console, with regular, bold, and italic variants and broad Unicode
support.

This SlackBuild enables Linux console fonts and selects the dotted zero
variant. It installs:

  * PCF fonts in /usr/share/fonts/X11/misc
  * OTB fonts in /usr/share/fonts/misc/uw-ttyp0
  * Linux console fonts in /usr/share/kbd/consolefonts
  * bdfmangle and project documentation in /usr/doc/uw-ttyp0-2.1

To choose another zero style, edit the `Digit0Dotted` selection in
`uw-ttyp0.SlackBuild` (for example, replace it with `Digit0Slashed`) and
rebuild the package. Other stylistic variants can be selected by
following the instructions in the `VARIANTS.dat` file.

Available variants and examples:

https://people.mpi-inf.mpg.de/~uwe/misc/uw-ttyp0/Variants.html

Refresh the font cache after installation if necessary with
`fc-cache -f`.
